  "title": "x or (y != z) pins, so it is NP-complete on cubic systems",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "The asymmetric knot x or (y != z), with signs and any order of places (12 relations), has a pinning piece with four internal points and five lines (the skeleton that also pins the Fibonacci law and parity), a pinned line x = 0 is a disequality, and a full piece exists; by the pinning theorem of ticket A and Schaefer, deciding it on cubic systems is NP-complete, so its failing cubic systems are coNP-complete to recognise. Checked: the pieces by enumeration, the reduction on 80 instances (cubic, simple, same solvability), failures on small cubic systems (exhaustive n = 4, 5; sampled n = 6, 8, 10), controls.",
